{"id":"6131b92d-aa5a-48b9-ba73-31f7eed7a775","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"2045925d90beb0db","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/fs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"03fa844ce8732bd753ab8e66e2544a31b86acb24","start":3655,"end":4184},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","toBytes","(","content",":","FileContent",",","encoding",":","string",")",":","Uint8Array","{","if","(","typeof","content","!==","\"","string","\"",")","{","return","content",";","}","switch","(","encoding",")","{","case","\"","binary","\"",":","case","\"","latin1","\"",":","case","\"","ascii","\"",":","return","Uint8Array",".","from","(","content",",","(","char",")","=>","char",".","charCodeAt","(","0",")","&","0x","FF",")",";","case","\"","base64","\"",":","return","Uint8Array",".","from","(","atob","(","content",")",",","(","char",")","=>","char",".","charCodeAt","(","0",")",")",";","case","\"","hex","\"",":","return","Uint8Array",".","from","(","content",".","match","(","/","..","/","gu",")","??","[","]",",","(","pair",")","=>","Number",".","parseInt","(","pair",",","16",")",")",";","default",":","return","new","TextEncoder","(",")",".","encode","(","content",")",";","}","}"]},"context":{"before":"967a080d2b81ad16","after":"8e069840af7cd086"}},"payload":{"text":"A string as just-bash means it: UTF-8 text, unless `encoding` says otherwise. Its pipes carry bytes as a latin1\nstring (a char per byte), and a redirect of a command's byte output (`base64 -d > x.png`, `cat a.png > b.png`)\nwrites it with `\"binary\"`: those chars are the bytes, and UTF-8 would turn each one above 0x7f into two.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:35.720Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:35.720Z"}
{"id":"71b21465-6626-41b9-92cf-6614ddaddb96","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b55475583bca3216","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/fs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"9f0331ad3ef90f20fdef4159f3ac2e03dff9bdbc","start":5350,"end":5745},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","resolvePosix","(","base",":","string",",","path",":","string",")",":","string","{","const","combined","=","path",".","startsWith","(","\"","/","\"",")","?","path",":","`","","${","base",".","endsWith","(","\"","/","\"",")","?","base",".","slice","(","0",",","-","1",")",":","base","}","/","${","path","}","","`",";","const","stack",":","string","[]","=","[","]",";","for","(","const","part","of","combined",".","split","(","\"","/","\"",")",")","{","if","(","part","===","\"","..","\"",")","{","stack",".","pop","(",")",";","}","else","if","(","part","!==","\"","","\"","&&","part","!==","\"",".","\"",")","{","stack",".","push","(","part",")",";","}","}","return","`","/","${","stack",".","join","(","\"","/","\"",")","}","","`",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"8e069840af7cd086","after":"297a7fe849588053"}},"payload":{"text":"POSIX path resolution — `path` against `base`, collapsing `.`/`..`. Pure arithmetic (no filesystem), so it\nsatisfies just-bash's SYNChronous `resolvePath` even though our store is async.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:29.920Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:29.920Z"}
{"id":"7993b8e7-42e7-487b-929b-b32bfe887694","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"1828db8391f53d25","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/fs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"a9843110a440f79c3bebab6f02f11518265b74f7","start":2028,"end":2042},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","FILE","=","1"]},"context":{"before":"c36977c20bb47eb8","after":"375abfba0aad4949"}},"payload":{"text":"vscode FileType bits (File=1, Directory=2, SymbolicLink=64) and FilePermission.Readonly (=1). Read numerically\nso this module needs no value import beyond the passed-in api.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:44.427Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:44.427Z"}
{"id":"79f77634-525a-43c4-8f33-599a4a8bd062","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"0006fd56a2171858","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/fs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"f058ad57b66e7d16f7cae6f2bcf8489b4960301d","start":1471,"end":1512},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["const","zenfs","=","callerFs","(","store",",","\"","terminal","\"",")"]},"context":{"before":"6d901488718f7e17","after":"b47c488cdae5d773"}},"payload":{"text":"The workspace's store as the terminal reaches it past VS Code: its calls the terminal's, in the store's counts.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:50.953Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:50.953Z"}
{"id":"7a1085af-43a9-4699-a9dd-6355c2c1a717","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"7b8f69553d45c7f1","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/fs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"1ab07db3a978745a107acf8cc98e4ae225fd9288","start":0,"end":98},"shape":{"type":"ImportDeclaration","atoms":["import","type","{","FileContent",",","FsStat",",","IFileSystem",",","MkdirOptions",",","RmOptions","}","from","\"","just-bash/browser","\""]},"context":{"after":"530ac57abe06ccac"}},"payload":{"text":"A just-bash `IFileSystem` backed by the editor's own filesystem (`vscode.workspace.fs`).\n\nThe terminal (just-bash — a pure-TS bash interpreter) writes through THIS, which routes to `workspace.fs` →\nthe workspace-fs overlay. Two things fall out for free by going through that single chokepoint rather than\njust-bash's default in-memory FS:\n• Permissions — a write to a managed/read-only config (see workspace-fs `readonly`) throws `NoPermissions`,\nsurfaced here as `EACCES`, so `> tsconfig.json` in the shell prints `permission denied` like a real shell.\n• Coherence — files the shell creates/edits fire the provider's change events, so they appear in the\nexplorer and are visible to tsserver; edits in the editor are visible to the shell. One filesystem.\n\njust-bash's FS interface is async, which matches `workspace.fs`. The ops vscode's FS API doesn't offer\n(symlink/readlink, chmod, utimes) degrade: symlinks are unsupported (thrown), chmod/utimes are no-ops — a\nshell `chmod` deliberately can't override a managed file's read-only-ness (that's the FS's call, not the\nuser's). The two optional interface methods (`readFileBytes`, `readdirWithFileTypes`) are omitted; just-bash\nfalls back to the required ones.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:53.973Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:53.973Z"}
{"id":"913ecc7d-d459-47d5-b3c1-798584e85a33","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"8e069840af7cd086","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/fs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"949508555c01cab06063f37d23c60ecd0f145d71","start":4529,"end":5146},"shape":{"type":"FunctionDeclaration","atoms":["function","fromBytes","(","bytes",":","Uint8Array",",","encoding",":","string",")",":","string","{","if","(","encoding","===","\"","hex","\"",")","{","return","Array",".","from","(","bytes",",","(","byte",")","=>","byte",".","toString","(","16",")",".","padStart","(","2",",","\"","0","\"",")",")",".","join","(","\"","","\"",")",";","}","if","(","encoding","!==","\"","binary","\"","&&","encoding","!==","\"","latin1","\"","&&","encoding","!==","\"","ascii","\"","&&","encoding","!==","\"","base64","\"",")","{","return","new","TextDecoder","(",")",".","decode","(","bytes",")",";","}","let","chars","=","\"","","\"",";","for","(","let","at","=","0",";","at","<","bytes",".","length",";","at","+=","8192",")","{","chars","+=","String",".","fromCharCode","(","...","(","encoding","===","\"","ascii","\"","?","bytes",".","subarray","(","at",",","at","+","8192",")",".","map","(","(","byte",")","=>","byte","&","0x","7F",")",":","bytes",".","subarray","(","at",",","at","+","8192",")",")",")",";","}","return","encoding","===","\"","base64","\"","?","btoa","(","chars",")",":","chars",";","}"]},"context":{"before":"2045925d90beb0db","after":"b55475583bca3216"}},"payload":{"text":"Bytes as a string in `encoding`, the inverse of `toBytes`. TextDecoder's \"latin1\" is windows-1252, which maps\n0x80–0x9f to other characters, so the byte encodings go a char per byte instead.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:32.775Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:32.775Z"}
{"id":"b5690964-5b34-4f0d-8e03-7ca314227472","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"42dd89f624bacead","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/fs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"e4c99927f88e64ccfc771b7e6c06a0b7df19bb57","start":10182,"end":10262},"shape":{"type":"ObjectElement","atoms":["\"","resolvePath","\"",":","(","base",":","string",",","path",":","string",")",":","string","=>","resolvePosix","(","base",",","path",")",","]},"context":{"before":"ae2028ac63bab1e4","after":"1031f7e42ed59523"}},"payload":{"text":"Synchronous helpers. `resolvePath` is pure arithmetic; `getAllPaths` walks the SAME store synchronously\nvia zen-fs (workspace-fs is zen-fs under /workspace) — the async vscode API can't answer a sync method.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:18.231Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:18.231Z"}
{"id":"ca2ccf90-5517-4168-afbc-8d756d985cfe","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b47c488cdae5d773","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/fs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"90f07beb82b9881d59f5c64551b196329df55e17","start":1634,"end":1690},"shape":{"type":"InterfaceDeclaration","atoms":["interface","EncodingOptions","{","\"","encoding","\"","?",":","string","|","null","}"]},"context":{"before":"0006fd56a2171858","after":"afa0c7d34e1778fe"}},"payload":{"text":"just-bash's `ReadFileOptions`/`WriteFileOptions` aren't re-exported from its `/browser` entry, so mirror the shape we use.","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:47.965Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:47.965Z"}
{"id":"cfe7c5c6-8333-4131-9aba-1313347e50be","kind":"note","ref":{"span":"b1cd93fccf551047","key":"bablr1","file":"packages/editor/workbench/terminal/fs.ts","baseline":{"blob":"cc9676f2fe30c2a19e245609a23fcb4a8d48f7a0","start":6796,"end":6844},"shape":{"type":"VariableDeclaration","atoms":["let","mode","=","0o","100000","|","(","writable","?","0o","644",":","0o","444",")"]},"context":{"before":"ca893742b5a00113","after":"9f359b7f9dfcee42"}},"payload":{"text":"A unix-ish mode for `ls -l` etc.: dir 0o755, file 0o644 (0o444 when the FS marks it read-only).","wrote":["Brian Jenkins"]},"author":"local","createdAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:23.906Z","updatedAt":"2026-11-22T18:06:23.906Z"}
